# SPA fallback — the whole reason a refresh on /login works.
#
# Brevé is one HTML file with a client-side router. Netlify only knows about
# /index.html, so a hard refresh on /login or /signup would otherwise be a
# genuine 404: there is no /login file on disk to serve.
#
# Netlify checks for a matching static file BEFORE applying this rule, so real
# assets (/assets/*, /favicon.svg) are still served normally and only unmatched
# paths fall through to the app. Status 200 rewrites rather than redirects, so
# the URL in the address bar stays /login for React Router to read.
#
# This lives in public/ rather than netlify.toml on purpose: everything in
# public/ is copied into dist/, so the rule travels with the build and applies
# whether you deploy from Git or drag the dist folder onto Netlify.

/*    /index.html   200
